Gavin77 wrote:
>
> I have spent about 3 months playing nethack on and off ...
> I have never gotten past level 10 in the dungeon ...

Then you are doing well.

> It is often hard to get your Pet next to the staircase in a dungeon
> Pets often do nothing when they are next to you and you have multiple
> monsters attacking you. They only seem to help sometimes ??

Pets are smart enough to only attack monsters weaker than
they are.  Players aren't that smart.  Two hints wrapped into
one!

> There are too many secrets walls/doors in dungeons. I find it virtually
> impossible to reveal everything on a level without getting hungry. So I
> often miss out on shops etc on levels. You can find and put a ring of
> searching on, but it doesnt always reveal things straight away. And you
> get more hungry if you wear magic rings.

Don't bother searching the entire level unless you have a good
reason to do so.  Levels with special features give messages
telling you about the level.  Learn those messages and watch
for them.  If you don't get the messages that say there is a
shop on the level don't search.

As to rings, yup that's the price okay.  Nethack is NOT a game
of exploration and combat.  It is a game of tearning and making
trade-offs.

> The biggest problem I have with hunger is that it is increased when you
> are using a magic ring or amulet. Could somebody tell me if wielding a
> magic weapon or if wearing magic armor increases hunger also ??

They do not, but.  Ah, there's always a but isn't there?
Objects have weight.  Carrying weight causes hunger.  As
long as you stay unburdened it does not increase your hunger.
So many hunger effects are indirect but they are there.

> It is way too easy to get your good items corroded. I have discovered
> that bashing acid and ocre jelly with my hands is better. But Gush
> Water traps are common, and there is no way of knowing the trap is
> there ??

Search, watch pets.

> I heard you can dip corroded weapons in potions of oil to fix
> them, but I am sure you cannot dip armor ?

No.  Not what oil is for.

> I heard you can grease your
> items to prevent this, but is it 100% proof against corroding ? Its not
> a good solution anyway, because the grease soon wears off? And any
> weapon you grease gets constantly dropped - not good while in a battle.

That's the trade-off.  Deeper down there is the Oracle.  The Oracle
wants a lot of money but the Oracle gives excellent advice.  Write
down any such advice and puzzle it through.  One of the advice
items given by the Oracle for the high money option is how to
handle corrosion.

As to acid monsters - Certain materials are immune to rust while
certain materials are immune to rot.  Pick the weapon that is
immune to the monster in question.  Some are obvious - a rubber
hose is immune to rust but subject to rot.  Some are NOT
obvious what material they are made off.  Experiment a bit and
figure out the non-obvious ones or since you have been reading
the spoilers pay close attention to the material in the tables and
be surprised there.  There's also learning which monsters inflict
which damage.



